Screenshots: schnitt-desktop-1440x900-scroll-0.png, schnitt-desktop-1440x900-mid-scroll.png, schnitt-desktop-1440x900-end-scroll.png, schnitt-desktop-1440x900-reduced-motion.png, schnitt-phone-390x844-scroll-0.png, schnitt-phone-390x844-mid-scroll.png, schnitt-phone-390x844-end-scroll.png, schnitt-phone-390x844-reduced-motion.png, schnitt-phone-390x780-scroll-0.png.
Phone shots in that commit: 390x844 at scroll 0, mid-scroll, end-scroll, and reduced motion, plus 390x780 at scroll 0. Desktop shots: 1440x900 at scroll 0, mid-scroll, end-scroll, and reduced motion.
Frame timing is in schnitt-frame-timing.json. Chromium, software WebGL, 4x CPU throttle, scrolling the hero for 1.2s.
390x844: 73 frames, median 16.70 ms, p95 16.70 ms, max 16.80 ms, share of frames above 20 ms = 0.
1440x900: 64 frames, median 16.70 ms, p95 16.80 ms, max 166.70 ms, share of frames above 20 ms = 0.02.
The earlier pair of numbers disagreed because a cutoff at 16.7 ms splits the 60 Hz cluster (frames land near 16.67 ms and a few at 16.8 ms) while a rounded p95 still prints 16.7. p95 here is the sample at ceil(0.95 n) - 1. Max is the slowest gap. Hero CLS 0. Console errors 0. Axe violations 0.
Not checked: a physical iPhone, and frame rate on that phone.
